assessment.verification_assessment:
Acceptance is observable and discriminating, and one independent verifier verdict on the exact candidate SHA is meaningful. The verdict covers four failure classes, each with an intact, fault and restored control:
(1) supervisor ownership is external to the model session and durably attributable to the monitor invocation;
(2) killing or stalling the monitor yields external detection and alert, and an authorized restart preserves generation and pending state;
(3) restart or observation with the wrong identity is refused, with no duplicate ownership;
(4) missing or invalid supervision or Doctor configuration holds before launch or restart.
The named pytest and node test commands give a starting surface; a full regression run is terminal only. Explicit non-claims (no live cutover or retirement) make over-claiming checkable. The key verifier judgment is whether the fixture uses genuine external supervision rather than an in-process or background-waiter stand-in, and the text states that criterion explicitly. The predecessor's DONE status is reported, not independently verified here.
